+# patches/
+
+Optional records of substantial repository changes, kept as unified diff files (e.g. `git diff > patches/NNNN-name.patch`).
+
+- They are reference material only: nothing applies them automatically, they are not part of any build or test run, and reproducibility never depends on them — the repository files themselves are the source of truth.
+- The team normally edits the repository directly; a patch file is worth keeping only when a change is large and a standalone record of it is useful.
+- Current contents:
+  - `0001-review-clarifications.patch` — the documentation corrections of 2026-11-10 (exact P7/P8 context counts, P6/P8 wording in the patch plan, A2 depth caps in the proposal, README A2 pointer, stale Gate 2 docstrings in `tests/test_ltb.py`, removal of the duplicate proposal file). Its edits are already in the working tree; the patch is the record, not the change.
+  - `0002-p7-baselines1.patch` — P7 (2026-11-11): the four Stage 1 baselines and run infrastructure — new `src/ub_rl/baselines.py` (enumeration, ordered scan, heuristic iteration, random search with checker-call accounting), `src/ub_rl/runstore.py` (result store with `status: "complete"` and `*_meta.json`; a result file without its meta file is rejected), `scripts/run_baselines1.py` (runs all 34,841 split contexts, asserts enumeration == ordered scan on every context), `tests/test_baselines1.py` (12 tests); README, `docs/how_to_run.md`, `docs/patch_plan.md` (P7 status) and `docs/verification_record.md` (P7 record) updated. Its edits are already in the working tree; the patch is the record, not the change.
+  - `review-P7b-fixes-on-c99614a.patch` — P7b (2026-11-11): review fixes to P7, committed as `b5aadf4` — random search seeded per (seed, context id) with nested budgets (budget 10 is a prefix of budget 20, and two contexts with the same seed get different subsets, both tested), the heuristic counts distinct sections, and the result store records `result_sha256`/`n_rows` and rejects edited CSVs; 7 new tests, `174 passed`. Record in `docs/verification_record.md`, section P7b.
+  - `review-P7c-record-full-run.patch` — P7c (2026-11-11): record of the full Stage 1 baseline run on all 34,841 contexts (project lead's machine) — acceptance criteria met, mean calls table, the heuristic matched the optimum in every feasible context, random-search gap summary; new `scripts/baselines1_summary.py` (store-validated summary) with a test; `docs/how_to_run.md`, `docs/patch_plan.md` and `docs/verification_record.md` (P7 full-run section) updated. Not yet committed.
+  - `0003-p9-landscape.patch` — P9 (2026-11-11): landscape and saturation diagnostics and the Gate 3 record — new `src/ub_rl/reward_checks.py` (five reward families and the float64 log-space ordering assertion with analytic margin bounds), `src/ub_rl/landscape.py` (monotonicity counter c1/c2/c2_block, all-pairs F1 action-graph distances, per-context diagnostics with `Checker.check` at the optimum), `scripts/landscape_diagnostics.py` (one script: per-set tables, the saturation table with V as the headline line and the ordered-scan row, the reward assertion on V, the script-rendered Gate 3 record, `--check` comparison, `--limit` samples, P7 snapshot assertion on full runs, runstore metas), and 25 new tests; `docs/how_to_run.md`, `docs/patch_plan.md` (P9 status) and `docs/verification_record.md` (P9 entry) updated. The 100-context sample is recorded; the full run and the committed `docs/gate3_record.md` are for the project lead.
